      "id": "the-demon-haunted-world-ch-13",
      "order": 13,
      "chapterNumber": 13,
      "headline": "Obsessed with Reality",
      "keyInsight": "We love stories that make us feel special and cozy. Reality, on the other hand, does not care about our feelings. It acts like a cold bathroom scale. You can stand on your tiptoes or hold your breath, but the needle points to the truth. Science is simply the stubborn habit of checking that scale anyway. It forces us to ask uncomfortable questions before celebrating comfortable lies. When we fall in love with fantasy, we build our lives on quicksand. The true thrill is not in make-believe miracles. It comes from uncovering how nature actually ticks right in front of our eyes.",
      "content": "Imagine driving across a desert with a gas gauge stuck on full. You can smile and feel relaxed, but you will still run out of fuel. That is the danger of tuning out reality. When wishful thinking takes the steering wheel, bad surprises wait just down the road.\n\nSagan shows us that genuine science is not cold or boring. It is the greatest detective adventure ever created. Instead of accepting rumors, scientists behave like careful building inspectors. They tap every wall, check the pipes, and test the foundation to make sure the house will not collapse during a storm.\n\nFantasies are fun in movie theaters, but living inside them leads to disaster. When we trade real testing for pleasant daydreams, we lose the ability to fix real problems. Looking at reality squarely in the face is not just smart. It is the only reliable way to build a future that lasts.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Embracing hard facts keeps your feet on solid ground when sweet illusions try to sweep you away.",
      "audioSnippetText": "Pleasant daydreams feel great until reality demands payment. Testing your world with honesty is the only way to build a life that stands tall.",
